# cryptomath-lab

**Educational cryptography & randomness lab** in Python. Showcases:
- A **toy Feistel network** (for intuition)
- **Simple PRGs**: linear congruential generator (LCG) and SHA256-counter PRG
- **Randomness tests**: monobit, runs, chi-square (bytes)
- A clean **CLI** (`cml`) built with Typer
- Tests with `pytest`, typed code, and docstrings

> This project is for learning/demo only — not production crypto!

## Quickstart

```bash
# create & activate a venv (optional but recommended)
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate   # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate

# install in editable mode
pip install -e .

# run tests
pytest

# explore the CLI
cml --help
cml prg sha256 --n 32 --seed "hello"
cml prg lcg --n 10 --seed 12345
cml feistel encrypt --key "mykey" --message "48656c6c6f" --rounds 4
cml test monobit --hex "aabbccddeeff"
```

## CLI Overview

- `cml prg sha256 --n 64 --seed "abc"`: generate 64 bytes via SHA256 counter PRG
- `cml prg lcg --n 16 --seed 42`: generate 16 bytes with LCG
- `cml feistel encrypt|decrypt --key K --message HEX --rounds R`: toy Feistel on hex input
- `cml test monobit|runs|chisq --hex HEX`: run simple randomness tests on byte stream

## Project Goals (What this shows on your CV)
- Clean package structure (`src/` layout), CLI, tests, and docs
- Clear, typed Python code with docstrings
- Reproducible results and unit tests
- CI workflow (pytest) for professionalism

